IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ml52-nouns`

-- Row il-52. THE TWO FINDINGS, as typed values.
-- A citation is encoded as TWO descriptions: what the citing words say they point at, and what the target is. A test compares them. Where they differ, the citation does not point at what it says;
-- that is a defect, kept in an expected-red file with its count declared in check.sh and encoding.json.
-- A numbered item is encoded as a record of its label, where it is placed, the first day it is read and how long. A test counts the items that bear one label on one day.
-- Two findings are recorded. Each has one sound control beside it.
-- DEFECT 1 (numbering): after item (18ח) of the First Schedule, an order of 2026 puts two items printed (18ט) and (18י) for two years, and an Act of 2026 puts a further item printed (18ט) from a later day.
-- CONTROL 1: the two items of the order bear different labels, and on any day before the Act's item starts every label names one item.
-- DEFECT 2 (citation): item (18ו) cites s 7ג(ב) of the Infiltration Law as brought in by s 1(1) of a temporary law of 2013; the consolidation prints that section as lapsed.
-- CONTROL 2: the order of 2016 that added item (18ו) says it comes directly after item (18ה), and the consolidation prints it there.
-- LIMBS. Limb (a) is the question whether the target is as the citing words say; limb (b) is the question whether the citing words still read so in the latest official text of the citing provision.
-- Each limb says where it was read from (see `Where a reading comes from` in ml52-nouns.l4). The Hebrew Wikisource text is not official.
-- A date for which the sources held give no answer is NOTHING; there is no REFUSE.

§ `Cross-references`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation points at what it says` MEANS c's `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS c's `the target is`

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs were read from the official instruments` MEANS
    c's `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    AND c's `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

-- Whether the text the citing words name is the text in force on a day. The only answer the sources held can give is the day it stopped being in force and the days from then on; for any earlier day,
-- and for a citation with no recorded end, the answer is NOTHING (fork D1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the named text is in force on` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the text the citing words name stopped being the text in force on`
        WHEN JUST stopped THEN IF day AT LEAST stopped THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the consolidation prints the named text as in force` MEANS NOT c's `the consolidation prints the named text as lapsed`

§ `Numbered items`

-- Whether an item is certainly not over on a day. An item with no end in its instrument is never over; an item read for two years is certainly not over before the first day it could be over;
-- from that day on the sources held do not say, so NOTHING (fork P1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN item IS A `A schedule item`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the item is certainly not over on` MEANS
    IF item's `how long it is read` EQUALS `to no end that the instrument which adds it states`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER item's `the first day it could be over`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST lowest THEN IF day AT LEAST lowest THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Whether an item is certainly read on a day: JUST FALSE before its first day, JUST TRUE from its first day while it is certainly not over, otherwise NOTHING.
GIVEN item IS A `A schedule item`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the item is certainly read on` MEANS
    CONSIDER item's `the first day it is read`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST first THEN IF day AT LEAST first THEN `the item is certainly not over on` item day ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN a IS A `A schedule item`
      b IS A `A schedule item`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`two items are certainly read on the day and bear one label` MEANS
    `the item is certainly read on` a day EQUALS JUST TRUE
    AND `the item is certainly read on` b day EQUALS JUST TRUE
    AND a's `the label printed` EQUALS b's `the label printed`

GIVEN item IS A `A schedule item`
      label IS A STRING
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if the item bears the label and is certainly read on the day` MEANS
    IF item's `the label printed` EQUALS label AND `the item is certainly read on` item day EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN 1
    ELSE 0

GIVEN label IS A STRING
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of recorded items that bear the label and are certainly read on` MEANS
    `one if the item bears the label and is certainly read on the day` (`item: first item of the 2026 order, label (18ט)`) label day
    + `one if the item bears the label and is certainly read on the day` (`item: second item of the 2026 order, label (18י)`) label day
    + `one if the item bears the label and is certainly read on the day` (`item: item added by s 27 of SH 3571, label (18ט)`) label day

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`two recorded items bearing one label are certainly read on` MEANS
    `two items are certainly read on the day and bear one label` (`item: first item of the 2026 order, label (18ט)`) (`item: second item of the 2026 order, label (18י)`) day
    OR `two items are certainly read on the day and bear one label` (`item: first item of the 2026 order, label (18ט)`) (`item: item added by s 27 of SH 3571, label (18ט)`) day
    OR `two items are certainly read on the day and bear one label` (`item: second item of the 2026 order, label (18י)`) (`item: item added by s 27 of SH 3571, label (18ט)`) day

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the labels are distinct on` MEANS NOT `two recorded items bearing one label are certainly read on` day

-- DEFECT 1. The numbering of the First Schedule after item (18ח).
-- THE ORDER. Kovetz HaTakanot 12422 (9 June 2026) p. 2196א, read from the page image: an order of the Minister of Justice with one operative section and no section on commencement.
-- Its signing date was run through the calendar routine, which reproduced 30 Kislev 5785 = 31 December 2024 first: 23 Sivan 5786 = 8 June 2026, and the issue's date 24 Sivan 5786 = 9 June 2026.
